  "analysis": "The policy explicitly requires obtaining **explicit user confirmation** before taking any action that updates the database or retrieves sensitive order details. The user in **h2** and **h8** requested changes to **two items** (coffee machine and laptop) but did not specify which of the three orders (#W5838674, #W4284542, #W2782744) they intended to modify. The assistant made **three tool calls** (`get_order_details`) for all orders **without confirming the correct order ID or obtaining explicit user confirmation**, violating the policy. The user also explicitly stated the order was **delivered**, but no confirmation was sought before proceeding.",

